# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never commit a credential value. See SECURITY in README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build + deps
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bake-off outputs.
#
# results/raw holds unaggregated per-run transcripts and ledgers. They are
# large, they are regenerated by a re-run, and they are the artefacts most
# likely to contain an un-redacted credential if the redaction chokepoint is
# ever bypassed. Aggregated results (results/*.json) are intentionally NOT
# ignored: they are the measured record the decision rule is applied to.
#
# acceptance/generated holds the sealed, frozen acceptance suites. Constraint 1
# of the protocol (doc 03 section 7.4): no builder may read, list or modify the
# suite. Keeping it out of the repo keeps it out of any workspace clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/raw/
#
# THE WHOLE OF acceptance/ IS IGNORED, not just acceptance/generated/.
#
# Integration finding: the sealed-suite root had three different spellings
# across four modules, and the campaign's default (`./acceptance`) fell OUTSIDE
# the single ignored subdirectory. One `--acceptance` flag, or one module
# disagreeing about the default, and every held-out test file lands in a
# committed path. Constraint 1 does not survive being one flag away from a
# `git add -A`. The pattern is now the parent, so no spelling of the root
# beneath it can escape.
acceptance/

# The dry-run tree. Regenerated by `npm run bakeoff -- dry-run`; holds a frozen
# throwaway suite and a REPORT.md built from INVENTED token counts. Committing
# it would put a document that looks exactly like a bake-off result into the
# repository.
dry-run/

# The scorer-mode proof tree. Regenerated by `node test/scorer-modes.e2e.mjs`,
# which freezes two throwaway suites and scores two hand-written artefacts.
# Holds held-out test files and score records that are not measurements.
.scorer-modes-e2e/

# The quality-gating proof tree. Same category, same reason: regenerated by
# `node test/quality-gating.e2e.mjs`, which freezes four throwaway suites and
# scores four hand-written artefacts to prove QUALITY-only failures no longer
# gate. Its score records are not measurements.
#
# It ALSO carries captures at
# `.quality-gating-e2e/*/results/screenshots/`, which the `results/screenshots/`
# rule above does NOT reach — that pattern has a middle separator, so it is
# anchored to this directory and never matches a nested copy. Every future proof
# tree has the same hole; ignore the tree at its root, as here.
.quality-gating-e2e/

# Sealed-scorer outputs (docker/README.md section 10).
#
# results/screenshots holds captures. Masking is applied at capture time and is
# the only masking there is — doc 02 section 1.7 residual risk 5: a secret
# rendered by a selector nobody anticipated is in the pixels permanently, and no
# later commit can un-publish it. Never version them.
#
# results/staging holds copies of build artefacts, results/scorer-out holds raw
# container output, and both are regenerated by a re-score.
#
# results/scores and results/tamper are NOT ignored: the ScoreRecord is the
# measured record the decision rule is applied to, and a tamper report is
# evidence that must survive.
results/screenshots/
results/staging/
results/scorer-out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.log
